-- title:
--   The $\ell$-shrinking as the intersection of all translates by vectors of length at most $\ell$
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a normed additive commutative group, let $S \subseteq E$ and let $\ell \ge 0$. Writing $S[\xi] = \{\,y : y - \xi \in S\,\} = \xi + S$ and
--   $$S_\ell \;=\; \{\,y \in S : \bar B_\ell(y) \subseteq S\,\},$$
--   one has
--   $$S_\ell \;=\; \bigcap_{\xi \in \bar B_\ell(0)} S[\xi] ,$$
--   the intersection being taken over all $\xi \in E$ with $\|\xi\| \le \ell$.
--
--   This identifies the shrinking, defined by a clearance condition on each point, with an intersection of translates — a description that converts a pointwise geometric requirement into a stable one under perturbation of the base point, and which is the form in which shrinkings are manipulated in later arguments. The hypothesis $\ell \ge 0$ is needed: for negative $\ell$ the closed ball on the right would be empty while the left-hand side is not the whole space.
